    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d119">

                <pb facs="0238" n="148" sameAs="frus:frus1934v03/pg148"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/6629: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-04-30T13:00:00+09:00">April 30, 1934—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received April 30—1:40 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>84. My 83, April 29, 7 p.m.<anchor n="80" xml:id="d119-f1"/> Despite previous
                    announcement by the Foreign Office spokesman that an official statement
                    clarifying Japan’s policy in China would be issued this afternoon, Amau said at
                    the press conference this morning that no such statement would be issued and
                    that he considered the affair “a closed incident”. No mention was made of the
                    American <hi rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire</hi><anchor n="81"
                        xml:id="d119-f2"/> presented to the Minister by me last evening.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
